@using System.Globalization
@using BlazorAtoms.RadialMenus

<PageTitle>AtomRadialMenu Playground</PageTitle>

<h1>AtomRadialMenu playground</h1>
<p>Tune <code>&lt;AtomRadialMenu&gt;</code> live. <strong>0&deg; is straight up and angles increase
   clockwise</strong>, like a compass. Item count is never capped &mdash; drag <strong>Item count</strong>
   up to 24 and watch the ring solve a bigger radius rather than overlapping.</p>

<div class="rm-docs">
    <h2>Terminology</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>Center button</dt>
        <dd>The button at the middle. Styled by <code>CenterSize</code>, <code>CenterShape</code>,
            <code>CenterColor</code>, <code>CenterBackground</code>, <code>CenterTemplate</code>. The
            geometry engine calls it the <em>hub</em> &mdash; it is the obstacle every item has to clear,
            which is why a sparse ring's radius is often set by the center button rather than by the
            items.</dd>

        <dt>Depth</dt>
        <dd>Nesting level. <strong>0</strong> is the root menu, <strong>1</strong> is a branch's
            children, and so on. Every item button carries <code>data-depth</code>. This is what
            "level" means everywhere in the docs. Capped at 16.</dd>

        <dt>Ring</dt>
        <dd>A <em>different</em> thing from depth: the concentric ring index <em>inside one depth</em>.
            It is only ever above 0 under <code>Overflow="RadialMenuOverflow.Rings"</code>, which wraps
            a crowded level onto extra circles. So an item can be depth 2, ring 1 at the same time.
            When you mean nesting, say <strong>depth</strong>.</dd>

        <dt>Slot</dt>
        <dd>One position on a ring. Holds either an item or a synthetic pagination stepper
            (<code>data-kind="page-prev"</code> / <code>"page-next"</code>).</dd>

        <dt>Path</dt>
        <dd>An item's address from the root: slash-joined indices, emitted as <code>data-path</code>.
            <code>0/2/1</code> means root item 0, then its child 2, then that child's item 1. Depth is
            the number of segments minus one. Two rings at the same depth under different parents are
            indistinguishable by <code>data-depth</code> alone &mdash; the path is what separates
            them.</dd>

        <dt>Branch / leaf</dt>
        <dd>An item with <code>Children</code> is a branch: it opens a ring and gets
            <code>data-branch="true"</code> plus <code>aria-haspopup</code>. Anything else is a leaf and
            raises <code>OnItemInvoked</code>.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Finding a deep path</h2>
    <p>Pick <strong>DeepTree</strong> as the item source: five levels, several children at every level,
       with the deepest path being <code>File &rsaquo; New &rsaquo; Project &rsaquo; Blazor &rsaquo;
       Server</code>. Turn on <strong>Debug</strong> and each item gets a tag showing
       <em>angle, radius and path</em>, on top of the arc bounds, ring circles, per-item ticks and any
       advisory the layout had to raise.</p>
    <p>In devtools, a prefix selector picks out a whole subtree:</p>
    <pre class="rm-docs-code">document.querySelectorAll('[data-path^="0/1"]')     // everything under root item 0, child 1
document.querySelectorAll('[data-depth="3"]')        // every item at level 3
document.querySelectorAll('[data-branch][data-expanded]')</pre>

    <h2>Loading children on demand</h2>
    <p>Pick <strong>LazyTree</strong>. Each branch fetches its children the moment it opens, with a
       latency slider standing in for the API call. Three fetch levels, then leaves, and
       <strong>reload data set</strong> throws the whole set away and starts over.</p>
    <p>Two things make it work. First, the component adds the path to its open set and rebuilds its
       rings <em>before</em> it awaits <code>OnBranchOpened</code> &mdash; so by the time your handler
       runs the branch is already open, and handing back the real children just renders them. No
       second click.</p>
    <p>Second, an unloaded branch must carry <strong>one placeholder child</strong>.
       <code>IsBranch</code> is <code>Children is { Count: &gt; 0 }</code>, so an item with no children
       is a <em>leaf</em>: clicking it raises <code>OnItemInvoked</code>, never
       <code>OnBranchOpened</code>, and the default <code>CloseOnLeafInvoke</code> shuts the menu. The
       placeholder here is disabled so it cannot be clicked itself.</p>
    <p>Use <code>Id</code> or <code>Data</code> to say which branch to fill, and put the children back
       at the <strong>same index</strong> &mdash; open paths are positional, so reordering during a
       reload moves whichever branch was open.</p>
    <p>Before swapping a data set wholesale, collapse. <strong>reload data set</strong> calls
       <code>CollapseAllAsync()</code> through <code>@@ref</code>, which is the only way to reset the
       expansion state under <code>Trigger="Always"</code>: that trigger pins the ring open, so the
       close path that would clear the open paths never runs. Skip it and branches stay expanded on
       paths into the old tree &mdash; the next click on one closes it instead of loading it.</p>

    <h2>Size grows fast with depth</h2>
    <p>Footprint is driven by depth &times; children per level &times; <code>ExpandMode</code>, and the
       three modes diverge sharply once you are more than two levels down:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Cascade</strong> &mdash; children radiate from the branch itself. Reads best, grows
            worst: by level 4 it is very wide, and <strong>sibling subtrees can genuinely overlap</strong>
            because each branch is solved on its own. Turn on <strong>Debug</strong> and the advisory list
            names the overlapping pair by path, with how far apart they are and how far apart they needed
            to be.</li>
        <li><strong>Concentric</strong> &mdash; one more ring radius per level from a shared center, each
            child confined to its parent's slice. Cannot overlap: a child ring is floored a whole
            <code>RingGap</code> outside its parent's radius. Compact for two or three levels,
            off-screen by four or five, and the slices get thin fast.</li>
        <li><strong>Drill</strong> &mdash; children replace the ring, and the center button goes back
            <em>and names the level you are on</em>. <strong>The only mode with a bounded footprint at
            any depth</strong>, at the cost of losing sight of the parent. Use it for genuinely deep
            trees.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Levers when it gets too big: <code>SizeScalePerDepth</code> (shrinks each level),
       <code>ChildSweep</code> (narrows the fan), <code>MaxRadius</code> with an
       <code>Overflow</code> policy, and <code>LabelPlacement="TooltipOnly"</code> to drop label-driven
       sizing entirely. <code>--radialmenu-extent</code> on the root reports half the box the open menu
       actually wants.</p>

    <h2>Why Concentric runs away, and the one lever that fixes it</h2>
    <p>Keeping a child inside its parent's slice means each level's arc is the parent's divided by the
       branching factor. Equal-size items on a narrowing arc need
       <code>R &ge; (ItemSize + ItemGap) / (2&middot;sin(arc/2))</code>, so <strong>the radius roughly
       doubles per level</strong> once that term overtakes the <code>RingGap</code> floor. With a
       180&deg; root arc and three-way branching the crossover is at level 3: radii go
       64, 126, 183, <strong>329</strong>, 604.</p>
    <p>No <code>ArcMode</code> changes that. <code>InheritSweep</code> keeps the radius linear but
       gives every level the full arc, so a deep item sits nowhere near its parent and the spokes
       become long lines to nowhere &mdash; it trades the symptom for a worse one. Shrinking items
       cannot keep up either, because <code>MinItemSize</code> floors them long before the arc stops
       halving.</p>
    <p>The fix is <strong><code>MaxVisibleDepth</code></strong>: cap the levels on screen and the arc
       can only narrow that many times, so the radius is bounded by construction. The menu
       <em>re-roots</em> &mdash; open deeper and the ancestor that scrolls out of the window becomes
       the center button, which names it and goes back. At the default sizes <strong>3 is about the
       largest window still bounded by <code>RingGap</code> rather than by item collision</strong>,
       and 2 is comfortable. <code>Drill</code> is the same idea with a window of 1.</p>
</div>

<p><a href="playground/activityindicators">&larr; Back to demo</a></p>

<div class="rm-stage">
    <AtomRadialMenu @ref="_menu"
                    Items="@CurrentItems"
                    @bind-Open="OpenV"
                    StartAngle="@StartAngleV"
                    EndAngle="@EndAngleV"
                    Distribution="@DistributionV"
                    AngleStep="@NzD(AngleStepV)"
                    Direction="@DirectionV"
                    Radius="@NzD(RadiusV)"
                    RadiusMode="@RadiusModeV"
                    MaxRadius="@NzD(MaxRadiusV)"
                    RingGap="@RingGapV"
                    ItemGap="@ItemGapV"
                    Overflow="@OverflowV"
                    MaxPerRing="@NzI(MaxPerRingV)"
                    PageSize="@PageSizeV"
                    VisibleCount="@VisibleCountV"
                    CrowdingWarnThreshold="@CrowdingV"
                    MaxVisibleDepth="@NzI(MaxVisibleDepthV)"
                    CenterSize="@CenterSizeV"
                    ItemSize="@ItemSizeV"
                    MinItemSize="@MinItemSizeV"
                    SizeMode="@SizeModeV"
                    SizeScalePerDepth="@SizeScaleV"
                    SizeStep="@SizeStepV"
                    FontSize="@FontSizeV"
                    LineHeight="@LineHeightV"
                    CharWidthRatio="@CharWidthRatioV"
                    TextFitFactor="@TextFitFactorV"
                    CenterShape="@CenterShapeV"
                    ItemShape="@ItemShapeV"
                    ShapeSides="@NzI(ShapeSidesV)"
                    ShapeRotation="@ShapeRotationV"
                    CustomPath="@Nz(CustomPathV)"
                    LabelPlacement="@LabelPlacementV"
                    ShowLabels="@ShowLabelsV"
                    MaxLabelChars="@NzI(MaxLabelCharsV)"
                    LabelOffset="@LabelOffsetV"
                    Trigger="@TriggerV"
                    ExpandMode="@ExpandModeV"
                    ArcMode="@ArcModeV"
                    ChildSweep="@ChildSweepV"
                    SingleBranchOpen="@SingleBranchOpenV"
                    CloseOnLeafInvoke="@CloseOnLeafInvokeV"
                    CloseOnOutsideClick="@CloseOnOutsideClickV"
                    HoverCloseDelay="@HoverCloseDelayV"
                    SpokeMode="@SpokeModeV"
                    SpokeWidth="@SpokeWidthV"
                    SpokeColor="@Nz(SpokeColorV)"
                    ItemColor="@Nz(ItemColorV)"
                    ItemBackground="@Nz(ItemBackgroundV)"
                    ItemBorderColor="@Nz(ItemBorderColorV)"
                    BorderWidth="@BorderWidthV"
                    CenterColor="@Nz(CenterColorV)"
                    CenterBackground="@Nz(CenterBackgroundV)"
                    HoverBackground="@Nz(HoverBackgroundV)"
                    ActiveBackground="@Nz(ActiveBackgroundV)"
                    LabelColor="@Nz(LabelColorV)"
                    DisabledOpacity="@DisabledOpacityV"
                    AnimationDuration="@AnimationDurationV"
                    StaggerDelay="@StaggerDelayV"
                    Easing="@Nz(EasingV)"
                    AriaLabel="@Nz(AriaLabelV)"
                    KeyboardNavigation="@KeyboardNavigationV"
                    Debug="@DebugV"
                    CancellationToken="@(CancelV ? Cancelled : default)"
                    ItemTemplate="@(UseItemTemplate ? BadgeTemplate : null)"
                    CenterTemplate="@(UseCenterTemplate ? StarCenter : null)"
                    OnItemInvoked="@OnInvoked"
                    OnBranchOpened="@OnOpened"
                    OnBranchClosed="@OnClosed"
                    CssClass="@Nz(HatchClass)"
                    Style="@Nz(HatchStyle)"
                    title="@Nz(HatchTitle)" />
</div>

<div class="rm-readout">
    <span>Open = <code>@OpenV</code></span>
    <span>Items = <code>@CurrentItems.Count</code></span>
    <span>Last event: <code>@(LastEvent ?? "(none)")</code></span>
    @if (SourceV == ItemSource.LazyTree)
    {
        <span>Fetches = <code>@_lazyFetches</code></span>
        <span>@(_lazyBusy is null ? "idle" : $"loading {_lazyBusy}…")</span>
        <button type="button" class="rm-clear" @onclick="ReloadLazyData">reload data set</button>
    }
    <button type="button" class="rm-clear" @onclick="@(() => LastEvent = null)">clear</button>
</div>

<div class="rm-controls">
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Item source (Items)</label>
        <select @bind="SourceV">
            @foreach (var s in Sources) { <option value="@s">@s</option> }
        </select>
        <span class="hint">@SourceHint</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Fetch latency, ms (LazyTree) <span class="val">@LazyDelayV</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="1500" step="100" @bind="LazyDelayV" @bind:event="oninput" />
        <span class="hint">Stands in for the API call. The branch is already open while this runs, so the
            placeholder is what the user sees.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Item count &mdash; crowding stress <span class="val">@CountV</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="24" step="1" @bind="CountV" @bind:event="oninput" />
        <span class="hint">Only affects the flat sources. The radius grows; nothing is dropped.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="ctrl group">Arc</div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>StartAngle <span class="val">@StartAngleV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="360" step="5" @bind="StartAngleV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>EndAngle <span class="val">@EndAngleV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="360" step="5" @bind="EndAngleV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Distribution</label>
        <select @bind="DistributionV">
            @foreach (var d in Distributions) { <option value="@d">@d</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>AngleStep (FixedStep only)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="AngleStepV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(unset)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Direction</label>
        <select @bind="DirectionV">
            @foreach (var d in Directions) { <option value="@d">@d</option> }
        </select>
    </div>

    <div class="ctrl group">Radius &amp; overflow</div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>RadiusMode</label>
        <select @bind="RadiusModeV">
            @foreach (var m in RadiusModes) { <option value="@m">@m</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Radius (px)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="RadiusV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(solved)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>MaxRadius (px)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="MaxRadiusV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(none / measured)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Overflow</label>
        <select @bind="OverflowV">
            @foreach (var o in Overflows) { <option value="@o">@o</option> }
        </select>
        <span class="hint">Rings/Shrink need MaxRadius (or MaxPerRing). Paginate and Spin always apply.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>MaxPerRing (Rings)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="MaxPerRingV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(derived)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>MaxVisibleDepth (levels on screen)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="MaxVisibleDepthV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(all)" />
        <span class="hint">Caps how many rings render, re-rooting deeper opens so the center goes back.
            The cure for a deep Concentric menu leaving the screen &mdash; try 2 with DeepTree. Ignored by Drill.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>PageSize (Paginate) <span class="val">@PageSizeV</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="12" step="1" @bind="PageSizeV" @bind:event="oninput" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>VisibleCount (Spin) <span class="val">@VisibleCountV</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="16" step="1" @bind="VisibleCountV" @bind:event="oninput" />
        <span class="hint">Scroll the wheel over the menu to rotate.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>RingGap <span class="val">@RingGapV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="48" step="2" @bind="RingGapV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ItemGap <span class="val">@ItemGapV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="48" step="1" @bind="ItemGapV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>CrowdingWarnThreshold <span class="val">@CrowdingV</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="2" max="32" step="1" @bind="CrowdingV" @bind:event="oninput" />
    </div>

    <div class="ctrl group">Size</div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>CenterSize <span class="val">@CenterSizeV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="24" max="140" step="4" @bind="CenterSizeV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ItemSize <span class="val">@ItemSizeV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="16" max="120" step="2" @bind="ItemSizeV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>MinItemSize <span class="val">@MinItemSizeV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="8" max="80" step="2" @bind="MinItemSizeV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>SizeMode</label>
        <select @bind="SizeModeV">
            @foreach (var m in SizeModes) { <option value="@m">@m</option> }
        </select>
        <span class="hint">FromFont estimates from the label; Measure asks the browser for the real width.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>SizeScalePerDepth <span class="val">@SizeScaleV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0.5" max="1" step="0.05" @bind="SizeScaleV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>SizeStep <span class="val">@SizeStepV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="16" step="1" @bind="SizeStepV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>FontSize <span class="val">@FontSizeV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="8" max="28" step="1" @bind="FontSizeV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>LineHeight <span class="val">@LineHeightV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0.9" max="2" step="0.1" @bind="LineHeightV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>CharWidthRatio <span class="val">@CharWidthRatioV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0.3" max="1" step="0.05" @bind="CharWidthRatioV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>TextFitFactor <span class="val">@TextFitFactorV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0.5" max="1" step="0.05" @bind="TextFitFactorV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>

    <div class="ctrl group">Shape</div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ItemShape</label>
        <select @bind="ItemShapeV">
            @foreach (var s in Shapes) { <option value="@s">@s</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>CenterShape</label>
        <select @bind="CenterShapeV">
            @foreach (var s in Shapes) { <option value="@s">@s</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ShapeSides (Polygon)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="ShapeSidesV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(6)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ShapeRotation <span class="val">@ShapeRotationV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="180" step="5" @bind="ShapeRotationV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
        <span class="hint">30 turns a hexagon flat-top.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>CustomPath (Shape=Custom)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="CustomPathV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="SVG path d, 100x100 box" />
    </div>

    <div class="ctrl group">Labels</div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>LabelPlacement</label>
        <select @bind="LabelPlacementV">
            @foreach (var p in LabelPlacements) { <option value="@p">@p</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>MaxLabelChars</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="MaxLabelCharsV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(unlimited)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>LabelOffset <span class="val">@LabelOffsetV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="32" step="1" @bind="LabelOffsetV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Toggles</label>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmLbls" @bind="ShowLabelsV" /><label for="rmLbls" class="inline">ShowLabels</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmTpl" @bind="UseItemTemplate" /><label for="rmTpl" class="inline">ItemTemplate (custom)</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmCtpl" @bind="UseCenterTemplate" /><label for="rmCtpl" class="inline">CenterTemplate (custom)</label></div>
    </div>

    <div class="ctrl group">Behaviour</div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Trigger</label>
        <select @bind="TriggerV">
            @foreach (var t in Triggers) { <option value="@t">@t</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ExpandMode</label>
        <select @bind="ExpandModeV">
            @foreach (var m in ExpandModes) { <option value="@m">@m</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ArcMode</label>
        <select @bind="ArcModeV">
            @foreach (var m in ArcModes) { <option value="@m">@m</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ChildSweep <span class="val">@ChildSweepV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="20" max="360" step="10" @bind="ChildSweepV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>HoverCloseDelay (ms) <span class="val">@HoverCloseDelayV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="1200" step="50" @bind="HoverCloseDelayV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
        <span class="hint">Trigger=Hover only. Items sit outside the host box, so the pointer crosses
            unowned space to reach them; without a grace period the ring closes before you arrive.
            Drag to 0 to see the bug.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Flags</label>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmOpen" @bind="OpenV" /><label for="rmOpen" class="inline">Open (two-way)</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmSbo" @bind="SingleBranchOpenV" /><label for="rmSbo" class="inline">SingleBranchOpen</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmClose" @bind="CloseOnLeafInvokeV" /><label for="rmClose" class="inline">CloseOnLeafInvoke</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmOut" @bind="CloseOnOutsideClickV" /><label for="rmOut" class="inline">CloseOnOutsideClick</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmKeys" @bind="KeyboardNavigationV" /><label for="rmKeys" class="inline">KeyboardNavigation</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmDbg" @bind="DebugV" /><label for="rmDbg" class="inline">Debug</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="rmCancel" @bind="CancelV" /><label for="rmCancel" class="inline">CancellationToken (cancelled)</label></div>
        <span class="hint">A cancelled token collapses the component entirely &mdash; the whole menu disappears, centre button included.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="ctrl group">Look</div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>SpokeMode</label>
        <select @bind="SpokeModeV">
            @foreach (var m in SpokeModes) { <option value="@m">@m</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>SpokeWidth <span class="val">@SpokeWidthV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="12" step="1" @bind="SpokeWidthV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>BorderWidth <span class="val">@BorderWidthV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="8" step="1" @bind="BorderWidthV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>DisabledOpacity <span class="val">@DisabledOpacityV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
